<InstitutionalPage
  title="Data deletion"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="How to revoke Nuvellum Social app access and request deletion of associated data under Nuvellum’s control."
  intro="Nuvellum Social helps the publication share stories through its own Meta-connected accounts. You can remove the app's access or request deletion of related data."
  note="Data deletion enquiries: sam@nuvellum.news"
>
  <h2>What this covers</h2>
  <p>The Nuvellum Social integration is used to publish content to Nuvellum-managed Facebook, Instagram and Threads accounts. Related operational records may include account identifiers, published post identifiers, delivery timestamps, publishing status and limited technical errors. Nuvellum Social is not a reader-login service.</p>
  <h2>Revoke the app's access</h2>
  <p>Authorized account holders can revoke Nuvellum Social permissions from the appropriate Meta app or website permissions settings. On Facebook, review Apps and Websites in account settings; on Threads, review Website permissions. Removing access stops the app from using that authorization, but does not necessarily remove existing Nuvellum operational records.</p>
  <h2>Request deletion of data we control</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:sam@nuvellum.news?subject=Nuvellum%20Social%20data%20deletion">sam@nuvellum.news</a> with the subject “Nuvellum Social data deletion”. Include the affected platform (Facebook, Instagram or Threads), the relevant account username and a description of the data you want removed. Do not send passwords, access tokens, authentication codes or sensitive identity documents.</p>
  <p>We will review your request, verify your authority over the relevant account where necessary, and delete applicable data under Nuvellum's control or explain any records that must be retained. We will respond using the email address from which you contacted us. Data controlled by Meta must be managed through Meta's own tools and policies.</p>
  <h2>Website and newsletter data</h2>
  <p>For requests about Nuvellum's newsletter, reader analytics or other website information, consult the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
</InstitutionalPage>
